 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Makes the shot behave as if the camera hung on a loose, heavy gimbal. It works out how the camera really moved and plays that through a weight on a spring: when a pan starts the view drags behind, when it stops the view swings past and comes back, and turns tip the horizon into the curve before it rolls level again. A still shot stays exactly as it was.",
